Duplicate IP means two devices in the same Layer 2 broadcast domain are configured with the same IPv4 address.

Example:

Device A -> 192.168.1.10
Device B -> 192.168.1.10

This is illegal.It causes ARP chaos.
ARP does IP to MAC address resolution.

If Device C wants to talk to 192.168.1.10. It sends an ARP request and both device A and B respond with their mac addresses.
Due to this the traffic goes to either device randomly.

This causes
	Intermittent connectivity
	Flapping communication
	Session dropping

This is called ARP instability.

ARP table keeps changing MAC for same IP
ARP table can be checked using the command 
	ip neigh
